I guess it just really hurts.

712
00:31:16,624 --> 00:31:20,628
I started liking him in a romantic way,
I got too aggressive and pushed too hard,

713
00:31:20,712 --> 00:31:22,672
and now I've just screwed it all up.

714
00:31:25,925 --> 00:31:28,219
I'm not sure
I'm capable of a relationship.

715
00:31:28,303 --> 00:31:30,680
I've even started thinking
about dropping out.

716
00:31:31,389 --> 00:31:33,641
That's how much I've given up.

717
00:31:38,146 --> 00:31:40,356
I really want to fix this issue I have.

718
00:31:44,068 --> 00:31:46,154
But I've only got one week left in here.

719
00:31:52,619 --> 00:31:56,080
People are always gonna want
what they can't have, know what I mean?

720
00:31:56,164 --> 00:31:58,124
That's exactly what's happening here.

721
00:31:58,207 --> 00:32:00,793
I want them to click
a little bit better now.

722
00:32:00,877 --> 00:32:04,088
But now Sharan's saying
that she wants to drop out of school.

723
00:32:04,172 --> 00:32:06,174
Yeah, I'm getting worried about her.

724
00:32:06,257 --> 00:32:09,427
She's, like, starting to get
a little emotionally unstable.

725
00:32:09,510 --> 00:32:10,345
Right.

726
00:32:10,428 --> 00:32:13,348
If someone could step in to support her,
that might help her.

727
00:32:13,431 --> 00:32:16,225
Tai-chan was grilling her hard,
which was unusual for him.

728
00:32:16,309 --> 00:32:19,479
It was, yeah. It all goes back
to the race where he carried her.

729
00:32:19,562 --> 00:32:22,273
<i>Just when Tai-chan thought</i>
<i>he won the chance to go on a date,</i>

730
00:32:22,357 --> 00:32:23,358
<i>Sharan chose Rune.</i>

731
00:32:23,441 --> 00:32:25,360
<i>That's where it fell apart</i>
<i>for Tai-chan too.</i>

732
00:32:25,443 --> 00:32:26,527
Exactly.

733
00:32:26,611 --> 00:32:29,405
I feel like with the students
from group two…

734
00:32:29,489 --> 00:32:30,990
- Yeah?
- …we can finally sit back.

735
00:32:31,074 --> 00:32:33,159
The dating show
has finally begun, thank you.

736
00:32:33,242 --> 00:32:36,329
- How many times have we said that?
- I have to keep saying it.

737
00:32:36,412 --> 00:32:38,331
- Or it won't start?
- Or it won't start.

738
00:32:38,414 --> 00:32:39,624
- Got it.
- It's a warning,

739
00:32:39,707 --> 00:32:41,125
even though I'm saying "thank you."

740
00:32:41,209 --> 00:32:43,711
You know those signs, "Thank you
for keeping this restroom clean"?

741
00:32:43,795 --> 00:32:45,755
- Right, right.
- I see.

742
00:32:45,838 --> 00:32:48,216
Same idea.
So thank you to all the crew members.

743
00:32:48,299 --> 00:32:50,259
Now we can finally watch
an actual reality dating show

744
00:32:50,343 --> 00:32:51,928
- with the group two students.
- Look at that!

745
00:32:52,011 --> 00:32:53,763
- Look how he's bowing to you.
- Much appreciated.

746
00:32:59,060 --> 00:33:00,144
Man.

747
00:33:00,895 --> 00:33:03,272
- Oh, there they are!
- I really love these two.

748
00:33:03,773 --> 00:33:05,858
I wanted to go on that date so badly.

749
00:33:05,942 --> 00:33:07,652
- You really mean that?
- Yeah. Sure.

750
00:33:07,735 --> 00:33:09,862
What? I wanted to.

751
00:33:09,946 --> 00:33:10,905
Really?

752
00:33:10,989 --> 00:33:13,574
Well, my mind is pretty much
made up already.

753
00:33:14,450 --> 00:33:16,285
What do you mean by "pretty much"?

754
00:33:16,369 --> 00:33:19,831
Is it between two people,
or are you like 90% sure on one guy?

755
00:33:19,914 --> 00:33:21,833
- Uh-huh.
- Well? Which one?

756
00:33:23,418 --> 00:33:25,837
- 90%
- Oh, the latter.

757
00:33:25,920 --> 00:33:27,130
- Mmm-hmm.
- I see.

758
00:33:28,589 --> 00:33:30,216
Who would you have picked today?

759
00:33:30,717 --> 00:33:33,094
- What do you mean?
- If you'd won the game.

760
00:33:33,177 --> 00:33:35,013
Well, I would've picked you.

761
00:33:35,096 --> 00:33:36,514
- <i>Whoa!</i>
- <i>Okay!</i>

762
00:33:36,597 --> 00:33:38,808
- <i>She said it.</i>
- What?

763
00:33:39,475 --> 00:33:41,477
Why are you smirking like that?

764
00:33:41,561 --> 00:33:43,438
- I didn't do anything. Huh?
- I thought you were cute.

765
00:33:43,521 --> 00:33:45,356
- You're cute.
- Oh. Thanks.

766
00:33:45,440 --> 00:33:46,357
Of course.

767
00:33:47,483 --> 00:33:50,445
I thought she'd tell it to him
straight today, but I guess not.

768
00:33:50,528 --> 00:33:52,196
Exactly.

769
00:33:52,280 --> 00:33:53,656
- It feels more true this way.
- It does.

770
00:33:53,740 --> 00:33:55,992
If she said it every time,
it'd feel forced.

771
00:33:56,075 --> 00:33:56,909
Right.

772
00:33:57,827 --> 00:33:59,704
- Sara, can we talk?
- Sure.

773
00:34:00,788 --> 00:34:05,501
I was thinking I wanted to give you
my drawing sometime before graduation.

774
00:34:05,585 --> 00:34:06,711
- Okay.
- Just for you.

775
00:34:06,794 --> 00:34:08,087
- Seriously?
- Uh-huh, yeah.

776
00:34:08,171 --> 00:34:09,464
- Really?
- Yeah.

777
00:34:09,547 --> 00:34:11,507
- But I can't draw portraits or anything.
- Okay.

778
00:34:11,591 --> 00:34:13,259
I haven't done much sketching,

779
00:34:13,342 --> 00:34:15,803
but I'm studying
Japanese-style designs right now.

780
00:34:16,345 --> 00:34:19,599
So, I wanna design
a traditional Japanese back tattoo.

781
00:34:20,224 --> 00:34:22,977
I mean, I draw that kind of thing
all the time anyway,

782
00:34:23,061 --> 00:34:25,396
so I wanted to give you one as a gift.

783
00:34:27,356 --> 00:34:30,693
I've never been given
a gift like that before, like, ever.

784
00:34:30,777 --> 00:34:33,488
- Oh, yeah?
- Never. Nobody does that.

785
00:34:34,030 --> 00:34:35,364
I think it's really sweet.

786
00:34:36,365 --> 00:34:40,036
Wow, this is crazy, I'm excited.
It's something more to look forward to.

787
00:34:45,500 --> 00:34:47,376
- Should we eat?
- Yeah.

788
00:34:47,960 --> 00:34:50,338
- Okay, hands together.
- Okay.

789
00:34:50,421 --> 00:34:52,173
- Let's eat!
- Let's eat!

790
00:34:52,256 --> 00:34:53,216
Let's eat.

791
00:35:02,517 --> 00:35:03,351
Mmm, yum!

792
00:35:03,434 --> 00:35:05,019
- This is so good.
- Mmm.

793
00:35:12,819 --> 00:35:13,778
How's it going?

794
00:35:14,403 --> 00:35:16,322
- We made good progress.
- Yeah?

795
00:35:16,405 --> 00:35:18,616
- We made a lot of food.
- The <i>takoyaki </i>is tasting great.

796
00:35:18,699 --> 00:35:20,284
Yeah, the <i>takoyaki </i>was amazing.

797
00:35:20,368 --> 00:35:22,453
- Should be good.
- I know, right?

798
00:35:22,537 --> 00:35:23,496
So good.

799
00:35:25,456 --> 00:35:27,041
- We're back.
- Hey, welcome back.

800
00:35:27,125 --> 00:35:28,167
- Hey.
- Hey.

801
00:35:28,251 --> 00:35:30,920
- Hey, you want some dinner?
- Not for you.

802
00:35:31,003 --> 00:35:32,463
- Did you eat?
- We did.

803
00:35:33,047 --> 00:35:34,841
But seeing as you made it,
I'll have a bite.

804
00:35:34,924 --> 00:35:36,634
- Me too.
- Don't do that.

805
00:35:37,760 --> 00:35:40,138
If you're going to half-ass it,
don't bother.

806
00:35:40,221 --> 00:35:41,180
- Huh?
- Oh.

807
00:35:41,264 --> 00:35:43,724
- That had a bit of an edge to it.
- Yeah.

808
00:35:44,308 --> 00:35:45,685
- Tell us about your date.
- Yeah.

809
00:35:45,768 --> 00:35:47,562
- For sure.
- Why are you grinning like that?

810
00:35:47,645 --> 00:35:49,522
No, I… I don't know.

811
00:35:50,565 --> 00:35:51,732
I'm so jealous.

812
00:35:51,816 --> 00:35:53,442
Was it the first time you spent alone?

813
00:35:53,526 --> 00:35:55,695
- Yeah.
- We hadn't had a proper conversation.

814
00:35:55,778 --> 00:35:58,322
- That's nice for your first date.
- Sounds awesome.

815
00:35:58,406 --> 00:35:59,657
- I was nervous.
- It was.

816
00:35:59,740 --> 00:36:01,868
And the cafe was deep in the mountains.

817
00:36:01,951 --> 00:36:04,328
- It had a second floor, but it was quiet.
- Yeah.

818
00:36:04,412 --> 00:36:05,371
Not a single sound.

819
00:36:05,454 --> 00:36:06,914
- Oh, I see.
- So, yeah.

820
00:36:06,998 --> 00:36:10,001
What's with you two
not making eye contact? Like…

821
00:36:10,084 --> 00:36:12,253
They're not, are they?

822
00:36:12,336 --> 00:36:14,505
- No! What are you talking about?
- Nothing to tell.

823
00:36:14,589 --> 00:36:17,258
- It didn't go well, they're like…
- Can I take a photo of you two?

824
00:36:17,341 --> 00:36:18,551
A post-date shot.

825
00:36:18,634 --> 00:36:21,304
Show us how close you feel.
Pose like you like each other.

826
00:36:21,387 --> 00:36:22,763
What does that mean?

827
00:36:22,847 --> 00:36:24,682
No, perfect.
Show us how close you two are.

828
00:36:24,765 --> 00:36:27,226
- No, our heads didn't touch.
- Say, "Cheese."

829
00:36:27,310 --> 00:36:29,353
- Is this a one-sided crush?
- A one-sided crush?

830
00:36:29,437 --> 00:36:31,772
How's that?

831
00:36:31,856 --> 00:36:33,816
- So the date…
- Tell us.

832
00:36:33,900 --> 00:36:36,611
Anyway, we went and did this glass thing.

833
00:36:36,694 --> 00:36:37,820
- What's it called?
- The glasses?

834
00:36:37,904 --> 00:36:40,072
- We made glasses.
- Ryukyu glass?

835
00:36:40,156 --> 00:36:41,616
- That's it.
- I love Ryukyu glass.

836
00:36:41,699 --> 00:36:42,867
- It was dragon-like.
- Wow.

837
00:36:42,950 --> 00:36:45,786
- You blow air into it and shape it.
- Oh, I know!

838
00:36:45,870 --> 00:36:49,081
So we made glasses and bought
these little phone charms too.

839
00:36:49,582 --> 00:36:51,042
- Wow.
- For everyone?

840
00:36:51,125 --> 00:36:52,710
- No, for us two.
- Oh.

841
00:36:52,793 --> 00:36:55,338
"For everyone?" Seriously?

842
00:36:55,421 --> 00:36:57,715
- Would've been nice.
- Didn't bring us souvenirs?

843
00:36:57,798 --> 00:37:00,635
You guys could only think
about yourselves, huh? Whatever.

844
00:37:00,718 --> 00:37:02,887
He's like, "For everyone?"

845
00:37:02,970 --> 00:37:05,139
- Ow, that's hot.
- Was it fun?

846
00:37:05,223 --> 00:37:06,224
Yeah, after that…

847
00:37:06,307 --> 00:37:09,644
- Mimi isn't joining in the conversation?
- What does this mean?

848
00:37:13,981 --> 00:37:16,192
So, Rinrin, how was the date?

849
00:37:16,275 --> 00:37:17,401
I'm curious.

850
00:37:17,485 --> 00:37:18,569
Who, me?

851
00:37:18,653 --> 00:37:20,863
I mean, I… I had a good time.

852
00:37:20,947 --> 00:37:24,075
Um, I don't know how to say it.

853
00:37:24,158 --> 00:37:26,494
I felt like I could…

854
00:37:26,994 --> 00:37:28,913
finally relax after a long time.

855
00:37:28,996 --> 00:37:30,957
- Mmm-hmm.
- I felt really refreshed.

856
00:37:31,040 --> 00:37:32,166
Mmm.

857
00:37:32,250 --> 00:37:34,961
I got to hear a lot about Kamaken's story,

858
00:37:35,044 --> 00:37:37,296
and he listened to my story as well.

859
00:37:37,380 --> 00:37:39,340
I guess I'm glad I asked him out.

860
00:37:39,423 --> 00:37:40,591
Mmm.

861
00:37:40,675 --> 00:37:44,303
- How do you feel?
- How do I feel?

862
00:37:45,221 --> 00:37:47,098
- I'm interested in him.
- I see.

863
00:37:48,933 --> 00:37:51,519
- Hmm.
- Mimi, how do you feel about it?

864
00:37:52,186 --> 00:37:53,396
- Huh?
- Hmm?

865
00:37:53,479 --> 00:37:56,649
- Wow, that was sudden.
- No, we're going around the circle.

866
00:37:56,732 --> 00:37:58,234
You're being unusually quiet.

867
00:37:58,317 --> 00:38:01,153
No, it's just… seeing them
come back, grinning like that,

868
00:38:01,237 --> 00:38:03,114
got on my nerves a little bit.

869
00:38:03,197 --> 00:38:06,075
- Like, "Kamaken's all happy now."
- He was grinning.

870
00:38:06,158 --> 00:38:08,953
- He said he was interested in you.
- No, I mean…

871
00:38:09,036 --> 00:38:13,040
He's also a transfer student like me,
I'm sure that's part of why he's curious.

872
00:38:13,124 --> 00:38:16,127
- But I don't think he does casual.
- Yeah, that's true.

873
00:38:16,210 --> 00:38:19,547
I guess it depends on who else
notices me and what I do from here.

874
00:38:19,630 --> 00:38:21,048
- Yeah.
- Okay.

875
00:38:21,924 --> 00:38:22,800
MEN

876
00:38:22,883 --> 00:38:24,760
Kamaken, how was the date?

877
00:38:24,844 --> 00:38:26,429
Yeah. You talked a lot.

878
00:38:26,512 --> 00:38:28,264
- Well, today…
- Mmm.

879
00:38:28,347 --> 00:38:31,600
…we had a lot of fun,
kind of like we were kids, you know?

880
00:38:31,684 --> 00:38:33,311
- I see.
- We really had a good time.

881
00:38:33,811 --> 00:38:35,855
And did your impression of her change?

882
00:38:36,647 --> 00:38:39,191
- It did change a bit, yeah.
- Oh, yeah?

883
00:38:39,275 --> 00:38:42,820
I used to think she was intimidating,
like really bold and full-on.

884
00:38:42,903 --> 00:38:43,738
I get that.

885
00:38:43,821 --> 00:38:46,157
But I got to see
a different side of her today.

886
00:38:46,240 --> 00:38:49,076
- Oh, wow.
- So I see her a little differently now.

887
00:38:49,160 --> 00:38:49,994
Yeah.

888
00:38:50,536 --> 00:38:53,539
So, do you think that it could lead

889
00:38:53,622 --> 00:38:55,333
to romantic feelings, or…

890
00:38:55,833 --> 00:38:57,752
Hmm, well, I mean,

891
00:38:57,835 --> 00:39:00,296
if it has to be either yes or no,

892
00:39:01,422 --> 00:39:03,090
I'd say I'm leaning toward a yes.

893
00:39:03,174 --> 00:39:04,342
Ohhh!

894
00:39:05,259 --> 00:39:08,637
<i>That must have been</i>
<i>super tough for him to have to hear.</i>

895
00:39:08,721 --> 00:39:09,638
<i>Yeah.</i>

896
00:39:09,722 --> 00:39:11,390
BADLY IN LOVE
MARINE ACADEMY

897
00:39:11,474 --> 00:39:12,933
Morning.

898
00:39:13,017 --> 00:39:14,018
Morning.

899
00:39:14,101 --> 00:39:15,644
Good morning.

900
00:39:15,728 --> 00:39:18,105
- Are we sitting all spread out again?
- Morning.

901
00:39:18,189 --> 00:39:19,190
Have a seat.

902
00:39:19,857 --> 00:39:21,317
- Morning.
- What's up?

903
00:39:21,400 --> 00:39:23,736
- Hey, Rune.
- You look cute today too.

904
00:39:23,819 --> 00:39:25,071
<i>What?</i>

905
00:39:25,154 --> 00:39:25,988
Spread out.

906
00:39:26,906 --> 00:39:28,949
<i>Oh, no.</i>

907
00:39:29,033 --> 00:39:31,827
- I actually drew you, Mimi.
- I heard the drawing was of a guy.

908
00:39:31,911 --> 00:39:32,953
I drew that.

909
00:39:33,037 --> 00:39:34,080
- Right?
- Right.

910
00:39:34,163 --> 00:39:36,415
<i>Damn, I feel bad for her.</i>

911
00:39:36,499 --> 00:39:37,792
<i>I know.</i>

912
00:39:39,001 --> 00:39:40,711
<i>Good morning, students.</i>

913
00:39:40,795 --> 00:39:41,754
Morning.

914
00:39:41,837 --> 00:39:44,882
<i>We have</i>
<i>two important announcements to make today.</i>

915
00:39:44,965 --> 00:39:46,258
- What is it?
- I'm scared.

916
00:39:46,342 --> 00:39:48,094
- <i>For tomorrow…</i>
- Huh?

917
00:39:48,177 --> 00:39:51,180
<i>…we've planned</i>
<i>an overnight date for two of you.</i>

918
00:39:51,263 --> 00:39:52,973
Wait, for who?

919
00:39:54,767 --> 00:39:57,103
<i>Tomorrow, there will be a contest.</i>

920
00:39:57,812 --> 00:40:00,064
<i>Whichever guy wins the contest</i>

921
00:40:00,147 --> 00:40:05,194
<i>will be the one who gets to choose a woman</i>
<i>to go on the overnight date with.</i>

922
00:40:05,277 --> 00:40:08,280
- Got it.
- I'm definitely going to win this.

923
00:40:11,575 --> 00:40:12,785
<i>Huh? What?</i>

924
00:40:13,744 --> 00:40:15,162
- <i>Wait…</i>
- <i>What's this?</i>

925
00:40:15,246 --> 00:40:16,080
<i>Hey…</i>

926
00:40:24,004 --> 00:40:25,923
- Who's she?
- Who is this?

927
00:40:26,507 --> 00:40:28,175
- An overnight date!
- That's crazy.

928
00:40:28,259 --> 00:40:29,093
Where are we going?

929
00:40:29,176 --> 00:40:30,719
- That's crazy.
- It sounds good.

930
00:40:30,803 --> 00:40:32,847
- All of us?
- No way. Definitely not.

931
00:40:33,431 --> 00:40:35,641
It's a date.
The guys have to compete for it.

932
00:40:35,724 --> 00:40:37,768
- Oh.
- I wanna go.

933
00:40:38,561 --> 00:40:40,062
Wanna go?

934
00:40:40,604 --> 00:40:42,940
<i>The other announcement is…</i>

935
00:40:50,114 --> 00:40:52,366
- Yeah, I think so.
- Well…

936
00:40:52,450 --> 00:40:54,201
- Overnight…
- Wait, wait, wait.

937
00:40:54,285 --> 00:40:55,286
Huh?

938
00:40:56,036 --> 00:40:57,621
- What?
- Who's that?

939
00:40:57,705 --> 00:40:58,873
- Hello.
- Hey.

940
00:40:58,956 --> 00:41:00,916
- You surprised me.
- What the hell?

941
00:41:01,000 --> 00:41:02,543
I'm Kaho Chinen, the transfer student.

942
00:41:02,626 --> 00:41:05,379
- No way!
- Huh? Now? Out of nowhere?

943
00:41:05,463 --> 00:41:07,423
- That's crazy.
- For real? Holy cow.

944
00:41:08,424 --> 00:41:10,342
- Crazy.
- A transfer student now?

945
00:41:10,426 --> 00:41:11,927
- Nice to meet you all.
- So sudden.

946
00:41:12,011 --> 00:41:14,221
- Get her to introduce herself.
- Okay.

947
00:41:14,305 --> 00:41:15,973
- I'm from Okinawa.
- Really?

948
00:41:16,056 --> 00:41:17,224
- No way!
- Same as you.

949
00:41:17,308 --> 00:41:18,893
- Really?
